# The build context of the images in docker/Containerfile.
#
# The file lies at the repository root because that is the context the build
# runs with: the Containerfile copies go.mod, cmd/, internal/, db/ and web/,
# which are siblings of this file, and a builder reads the ignore file of the
# context - one placed next to the Containerfile would simply be ignored.
#
# It is an allowlist and not a list of exceptions: everything is excluded
# first and only the sources of the artefacts are let back in. A denylist
# would send every new directory to the builder until somebody remembered to
# add it, and the directories that must never enter an image - state, keys,
# environment files, the Vagrant laboratory - are exactly the ones nobody
# remembers. What is not named here does not reach the build, does not land
# in a layer and cannot be read out of the image afterwards.
**

!go.mod
!go.sum

!cmd/
!cmd/**
!internal/
!internal/**

# The migrations are embedded in the control plane binary, so the directory
# is a source of the build even though it is never copied into the image.
!db/
!db/**

# The panel: the manifests, the build configuration and the sources. Nothing
# else of web/ - node_modules is installed from the lockfile in the build
# stage, dist/ is produced there, and the end-to-end tests are not part of
# any artefact.
!web/package.json
!web/package-lock.json
!web/index.html
!web/tsconfig.json
!web/vite.config.ts
!web/public/
!web/public/**
!web/src/
!web/src/**

# The Containerfile itself, for a build that reads it from the context
# instead of through -f.
!docker/Containerfile
